    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d241-a3">

                <pb facs="0518" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg448"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 648.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Affidavit of Peter Groden.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center">[Office of the Commissioners of Emigration, Castle Garden,
                    New York.]</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">State of New York</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">City and County of New York, ss:</hi></p>
                <p>Peter Groden, being duly sworn, deposes and says: That he is a detective
                    connected with the municipal police of the city of New York, and that he made
                    inquiries at No. 533 West Twenty-sixth street, New York City, and in the
                    immediate neighborhood thereof, and could find no person by the name of Mary
                    Reardon, or any one else in the house No. 533 West Twenty-sixth street that knew
                    her. And that deponent spoke to several persons who reside in said house, who
                    replied that they never heard of any letters having been written to John and
                    Mary Clifford.</p>
                <closer><signed>PETER GRODEN.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Sworn to before me <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-08-02">this 2d day of August, 1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>OTTO HEINZMAN</signed>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Notary Public, New
                        York.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
